<h2>Estimation Exploration</h2>
<p><strong>Original 2021 learning goal:</strong> Apply understanding of measuring objects to the nearest half and fourth of an inch to create an Estimation Exploration activity.</p>
<p>Warm-up Estimation Exploration: Fractional Measurement (10 minutes). The original photo asks for an earthworm&#x27;s length, but the photo&#x27;s physical reference scale and pixel dimensions were not independently verified. Do not assert a specific worm length.</p>
<h3>Fractional Measurement: Estimate</h3><p>Review original earthworm image with teacher; without verified scale do not manufacture a length. Teacher evaluates actual cards, drawings, images, and oral work where required.</p>
<h3>Design Your Estimation Exploration</h3><p>Select a measured object; compose nearest-half- or quarter-inch question and estimates that are low/right/high. Teacher evaluates actual cards, drawings, images, and oral work where required.</p>
<h3>Facilitate Your Estimation Exploration</h3><p>Show the object, invite estimates and partner explanations, then record the class responses. Teacher evaluates actual cards, drawings, images, and oral work where required.</p>
<p>Original public source lesson: <a href="https://im.kendallhunt.com/k5/teachers/grade-3/unit-8/lesson-14/lesson.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2021 teacher material</a>.</p>
<p><strong>Original-source limitation:</strong> Original earthworm image pixels and calibrated scale are unverified. Publisher-gated Cool-down is not claimed.</p></section>
